# Weles conventions

## Language and privacy

- All code, comments, README, OpenAPI, ROADMAP, CHANGELOG, and `docs/` are **English**.
- **Never** name real integrating products, production domains, or consumer repositories in public docs, examples, fixtures, or committed config.
- Use only fictional examples: `example-app`, `app.example.com`, `user@example.com`.
- Real allowlists belong in deploy-time `WELLS_APPS_YAML` / gitignored `config/apps.yaml` / private notes — not in git.

## Scope

- Do not implement features outside the current ROADMAP version unless the user explicitly requests it.
- When starting a planned item, update `ROADMAP.md` status and add a `CHANGELOG.md` `[Unreleased]` entry.

## Code

- Prefer small packages, interfaces for Turnstile/SES, table-driven tests.
- Never log `message`, `email`, or Turnstile tokens.
- Email notifications are plaintext only (no HTML).
- No API keys as browser authentication.

## Releases

- Follow Keep a Changelog categories: Added, Changed, Deprecated, Removed, Fixed, Security.
- SemVer: features MINOR, fixes PATCH, breaking API MAJOR.
